## 6. Business Model: B.Y.O.C. vs. Managed

### The "Control Plane" (Hosted by Kloudlite)
This is the **Console** (`web/apps/console`) and the **API Server** (`api/cmd/server`). It handles Billing, Auth, and Team Management. Think of this as the "Headquarters."

### The "Data Plane" (Hosted by You - BYOC)
This is the **Operator** running on your Kubernetes Cluster. Think of this as the "Field Office."
-   **Bring Your Own Cloud (BYOC)**: You pay AWS/GCP for the servers. You install the Kloudlite Operator.
-   **Privacy**: Your code/data never leaves your cluster. The Operator only pulls config from the Control Plane.

