## 8. Detailed File-by-File Manifest

### Backend: `api/`

#### Entry Points (`api/cmd/`)
*   **`server/`**: The Control Plane API.
    *   `main.go`: Starts the **Gin** (a popular web framework for Go) server and connects to **Supabase** (an open-source Firebase alternative providing Database and Auth).
*   **`kl/`**: The Developer CLI tool.
    *   `main.go`: Logic for `kl login`, `kl intercept`, `kl env switch`.
*   **`kltun/`**: The Tunnel Daemon.
    *   `main.go`: Manages the WireGuard interface and **CA Certificate** (Certificate Authority - a digital ID card used to prove your identity for secure HTTPS connections) installation.
*   **`workmachine-node-manager/`**: A Kubernetes **DaemonSet** (a type of K8s app that ensures exactly one copy runs on *every single node* in the cluster).
    *   `main.go`: Runs on every node. Installs **Nix** packages (a powerful package manager that can install tools like Node, Go, or Python without polluting the rest of the system) requested by workspaces.

#### Controllers (`api/internal/controllers/`)
*   **`composition/`**: Manages "Apps" (groups of services).
    *   `intercepts.go`: The logic for injecting `socat` proxies.
    *   `deployment.go`: Logic for creating standard Kubernetes Deployments from your Kloudlite config.
*   **`environment/`**: Manages Namespaces.
    *   `env_cloning.go`: Logic for deep-copying an environment (e.g., for **PR Previews** - temporary environments created automatically when you submit code for review).
    *   `network_policy.go`: Configures K8s **NetworkPolicies** (virtual firewalls inside the cluster) to isolate environments from each other.
*   **`workspace/`**: Manages Dev Containers.
    *   `workspace_controller.go`: Creates the Pod where you SSH into.
    *   `networking.go`: Sets up the Headless Service that `socat` forwards to.

### Frontend: `web/`

#### Admin Console (`web/apps/console/`)
*   **`src/app/installations/`**: Pages for managing Cluster connections.
*   **`src/app/login/`**: Auth pages using Supabase.

#### Developer Dashboard (`web/apps/dashboard/`)
*   **`src/app/(main)/`**: Main app layout.
*   **`src/actions/`**: **Server Actions** (a Next.js feature that allows you to write backend code directly inside your frontend files) for mutations.

#### UI Library (`web/packages/ui/src/`)
*   `button.tsx`: Reusable Button component.
*   `dialog.tsx`: Modal dialogs.
*   `form.tsx`: **React Hook Form** wrappers (a library for managing complex forms easily).
